    {"model":"astra-pro","coverage":"substantive response to supplied excerpts only","content":"## Decision: preserve the demonstrated seed/sprout mechanism; reopen the layout rejection\n\nThe owner’s correction is supported by the supplied historical script:\n\n```sh\nbtrfs device add <writable-device> <mounted-seed-path>\n```\n\nThis is explanatory syntax, not an instruction to execute.\n\nThe immutable seed supplies backing; the added writable member supplies persistent sprout writes. Rejecting the complete Incus/subvolume arrangement because an exposed subvolume is not a block-device operand was an invalid layer conflation. That rejection must be withdrawn. This does **not** establish a proven no-loop replacement topology.\n\n## What the original script demonstrates\n\nSource: commit `26a4ad132fbbd4523b05724060bfdeb9ca661824`, `deploy/runit/libexec-3tched/op-identity-root`, supplied lines 1172–1196.\n\n| Stage | Direct evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Mount seed view | Line 1172 mounts `$seed_view` read-only at `$seed_dir/volume`, with `subvolid=5`. |\n| Preserve inherited layout | Lines 1175–1180 validate and record seven distinct sibling subvolumes. The inherited `@` has `ro=false`; that property does not negate the physical seed’s read-only enforcement. |\n| Protect seed | Lines 1181–1185 verify physical block read-only state, `SEEDING`, source FSID and generation. |\n| Record intent | Line 1187 records `device-add-intent` before membership establishment. |\n| Add writable member | **Line 1188 executes `btrfs device add \"$leaf_loop\" \"$seed_dir/volume\"`.** The operand is `$leaf_loop`, not an exposed subvolume and not Cozo metadata. |\n| Establish sprout identity | Lines 1189–1193 sync, unmount, extract the sprout FSID from `$leaf`, reject an invalid or unchanged FSID, and record `layout-intent`. |\n| Remount writable sprout | Line 1194 mounts `$leaf_loop` read-write at `$seed_dir/volume`, explicitly supplying both `$seed_view` and `$leaf_loop`. |\n| Verify preservation | Lines 1195–1196 verify the resulting volume and unchanged inherited sibling identities. |\n\nThese lines demonstrate the historical implementation sequence. They do not independently prove a successful execution, define how `$leaf_loop` and `$seed_view` were constructed, or show final Cozo adoption.\n\n## Distinct layers\n\n- **Seed backing:** immutable shared seed, with its own physical and filesystem identity checks.\n- **Writable member:** added once during explicit establishment; receives sprout writes.\n- **Cozo association:** records which identity owns the established storage. Metadata does not supply a kernel block device.\n- **Exposed subvolumes:** filesystem trees presented to the container. Their exposure does not require each tree to be the operand of `btrfs device add`.\n- **Upgrade replica:** separate from persistent sprout writes and from the seed itself.\n\nHermes message **4099** acknowledges the persistent-member versus writable-overlay-upper error. Message **4111** claims `prepare-instance-disk.sh:111` adds the root partition, lines 116–118 prepare the separate upgrade partition, and `bind-instance-root.sh:216` composes a read-only overlay. Those are **historical assistant claims with source pointers**, not direct script excerpts supplied to this panel. They must not be silently merged with the directly demonstrated `$leaf_loop` sequence.\n\n## Remaining constraints and required specification changes\n\n1. **No host loops is absolute.** Historical `$leaf_loop`, seed wrappers, and the recorded pool loop are conflicts to resolve—not exemptions and not authorization to detach anything.\n2. **Reopen feasibility, without declaring success.** Identify the actual historical seed/member construction and the supported no-loop backing primitives before selecting a topology. Neither Cozo associations nor native Incus filesystem-volume declarations alone prove preservation of seed/sprout semantics.\n3. **Preserve the existing workflow’s contracts.** Proposed changes must retain one-time membership establishment, durable intents, distinct sprout identity, inherited subvolume checks, immutable-seed verification, identity-bound adoption, separate upgrade receive/pairing and lifecycle restoration without membership churn.\n4. **Do not substitute semantics.** Copied roots, snapshot-based replacement, a writable OverlayFS upper, VM conversion or new LVM management are not established solutions.\n5. **Keep completion separate from implementation evidence.** Neither this script nor Hermes’s acknowledgment proves current storage establishment, authoritative adoption or startup.\n\n## Panel evidence and coverage receipt\n\n- Reviewed here: only the explicit correction, historical lines 1172–1196, and quoted Hermes messages **4095, 4099 and 4111**.\n- Not reviewed here: full histories, variable construction, Cozo implementation, recovery files or other panel responses.\n- This response represents **one advisory panel member**. Configured member identities and success/failure receipts are unavailable to this member; no panel consensus is claimed.\n- No JEV judgment, filesystem write, storage operation, implementation, build, deployment or test was performed by this member."},
